{"name":"Palmetto","hex":"#6d9a9b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Palmetto","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of places in the United States:\nAn unincorporated community in Pickens County, Alabama.\nA former community in Plumas County, California.\nA city and historic district in Manatee County, Florida.\nA city mostly in Fulton County, Georgia.\nAn unincorporated community in Oglethorpe County, Georgia.\nA village in St. Landry Parish, Louisiana.\nAn unincorporated community in Greene County, Missouri.\nA ghost town in Esmeralda County, Nevada.","An unincorporated community in Pickens County, Alabama."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Palmetto"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sabal","blocks":[{"text":"Sabal is a genus of New World palms. Currently, there are 17 recognized species of Sabal, including one hybrid species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/SabalPalm.jpg/330px-SabalPalm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sabal","wikidata":"Q132826"},{"title":"Sabal bermudana","blocks":[{"text":"Sabal bermudana, commonly known as the Bermuda palmetto or bibby-tree, is one of 15 species of palm trees in the genus Sabal and is endemic to Bermuda although reportedly naturalized in the Leeward Islands. It was greatly affected by the introduction of non-native plants such as the Chinese fan palm, which created competition for space that it usually lost."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Sabal-bermudana.jpg/330px-Sabal-bermudana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sabal_bermudana","wikidata":"Q738459"},{"title":"Palmetto (train)","blocks":[{"text":"The Palmetto is a passenger train operated by Amtrak on a 829-mile (1,334 km) route between New York City and Savannah, Georgia, via the Northeast Corridor, Washington, D.C., Richmond, Virginia, Fayetteville, North Carolina, and Charleston, South Carolina. The Palmetto is a shorter version of the Silver Meteor, which continues south to Miami, Florida. From 1996 to 2002 this service was called the Silver Palm. Although currently a day train, the Palmetto is considered a long-distance train by Amtrak and previously provided overnight sleeper service to Florida."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Southbound_Palmetto_arriving_at_Fredericksburg_station%2C_December_2018.jpeg/330px-Southbound_Palmetto_arriving_at_Fredericksburg_station%2C_December_2018.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palmetto_(train)","wikidata":"Q944742"},{"title":"Palmetto (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Palmetto is a 1998 neo-noir thriller film directed by Volker Schlöndorff from a screenplay by E. Max Frye. It is based on the 1961 novel Just Another Sucker by James Hadley Chase. The film stars Woody Harrelson, Elisabeth Shue and Gina Gershon."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2d/Palmetto_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palmetto_(film)","wikidata":"Q512176"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Sabalpalm_-_Kabanapalm_%28Sabal_antillensis%29_03.jpg/500px-Sabalpalm_-_Kabanapalm_%28Sabal_antillensis%29_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Sabalpalm_-_Kabanapalm_%28Sabal_antillensis%29_03.jpg/1280px-Sabalpalm_-_Kabanapalm_%28Sabal_antillensis%29_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Sabalpalm_-_Kabanapalm_%28Sabal_antillensis%29_03.jpg/500px-Sabalpalm_-_Kabanapalm_%28Sabal_antillensis%29_0